  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SECURING LIVELIHOODS AND REDUCING DEPENDENCE ON BIOMASS EXTRACTION FOR RECOVERY OF TIGER AND PREY POPULATIONS IN THE WESTERN GHATS, SOUTHERN INDIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO (1) PROVIDE COMPREHENSIVE SUPPORT TO MARGINALIZED FAMILIES RESIDING OUTSIDE PROTECTED AREAS (PAS) TOWARDS IMPROVING THEIR SOCIO-ECONOMIC STATUS AND MINIMIZING THEIR DEPENDENCE ON FOREST RESOURCES TO FACILITATE THE RECOVERY OF TIGER AND PREY POPULATIONS IN THESE FORESTS. THIS SUPPORT WILL INCLUDE ASSISTANCE WITH ACCESS TO BENEFITS UNDER VARIOUS GOVERNMENT SCHEMES TO ASSIST IN ECONOMIC DEVELOPMENT, ORGANIZING TRAINING PROGRAMS FOR THESE FAMILIES ON INCOME GENERATION PROGRAMS AND PROVIDING GUIDANCE ON IMPROVED FARMING TECHNIQUES, AND PROVIDING THESE FAMILIES WITH SEEDS, SAPLINGS AND AGRICULTURAL SUPPLIES (2) SUPPORT THE FOREST DEPARTMENT AND OTHER GOVERNMENT DEPARTMENTS IN THE MANAGEMENT, CONSERVATION AND ECOLOGICAL MONITORING OF TIGER AND PREY POPULATIONS AS WELL AS THEIR HABITATS AND (3) STRENGTHEN STEWARDSHIP FOR FORESTS AND WILDLIFE AMONG RURAL COMMUNITIES LIVING ADJACENT TO WILDLIFE AND WILDLIFE HABITATS.</narrative>
  </description>
